Sec. 3 (new RCW section in chapter 9.41): (1) No person in this state may manufacture, import, distribute, sell, or offer for sale any assault weapon, except as authorized in this section.
Sec. 3 (new RCW section in chapter 9.41): (2) Subsection (1) of this section does not apply to any of the following:
Sec. 3 (new RCW section in chapter 9.41): (a) The manufacture, importation, distribution, offer for sale, or sale of an assault weapon by a licensed firearms manufacturer for the purposes of sale to any branch of the armed forces of the United States or the state of Washington, or to a state or federal law enforcement agency for use by that agency or its employees for law enforcement purposes;
Sec. 3 (new RCW section in chapter 9.41): (3) A person who violates this section is guilty of a gross misdemeanor.
Sec. 2 (RCW 9.41.010): (2)(a) "Assault weapon" means:
Sec. 2 (RCW 9.41.010): (ii) A semiautomatic rifle that has an overall length of less than 30 inches;
Sec. 2 (RCW 9.41.010): (v) A semiautomatic, center fire rifle that has a fixed magazine with the capacity to accept more than 10 rounds;
Sec. 2 (RCW 9.41.010): (c) "Assault weapon" does not include antique firearms, any firearm that has been made permanently inoperable, or any firearm that is manually operated by bolt, pump, lever, or slide action.
Sec. 4 (new RCW section in chapter 9.41): (2) A violation of section 3 of this act is an unfair or deceptive act or practice or unfair method of competition in the conduct of trade or commerce for purposes of the consumer protection act, chapter 19.86 RCW.
